{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2fea8f0b61c6980","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019: Curated getting-started tutorial gallery\n10\t\n11\tThe strategy delivers a curated tutorial gallery in the Dashboard: product code\n12\t(the gallery and one-click launch mechanics), authored content (six curated\n13\ttutorials spanning notebooks and pipelines), and documentation. These are three\n14\tarchitecturally distinct work streams with different owners and review cycles,\n15\tso the strategy is decomposed into a multi-epic DAG rather than a single epic.\n16\t\n17\t## Epic List\n18\t\n19\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n20\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n21\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Define the tutorial packaging format | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Tutorial gallery and one-click launch in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Author five curated notebook tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Author the first-pipeline tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Document tutorial gallery usage and tutorial contribution | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n26\t\n27\t## Dependency DAG\n28\t\n29\t```mermaid\n30\tgraph TD\n31\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 Tutorial packaging format] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 Dashboard gallery and launch]\n32\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 Notebook tutorials]\n33\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 Pipeline tutorial]\n34\t    E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 Documentation]\n35\t    E002 --> E005\n36\t    E003 --> E005\n37\t    E004 --> E005\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t## DAG Justification\n41\t\n42\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n43\t|------|------|-----------|\n44\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The Dashboard gallery code builds against the packaging format (metadata schema, pinned images) to render and launch tutorials; the format is an API-like artifact, not a configuration reference. |\n45\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | Notebook tutorials are packaged in the format; authoring them against an undefined schema would force rework and duplicate the schema definition. |\n46\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged in the same format; same reasoning as E003. |\n47\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring epic blocked by all Implementation epics. |\n48\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the shipped gallery and launch behavior. |\n49\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation references the curated tutorial set. |\n50\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation references the curated tutorial set. |\n51\t\n52\tE002, E003, and E004 run in parallel once the format exists (Rule 14: different\n53\trepos/components, no shared artifacts beyond the format). No Investigation\n54\tepics: the strategy's Open Questions section is empty, and the remaining\n55\tunknowns (exact metadata fields, validation tooling details) are implementation\n56\tdetails the owning teams resolve, not genuine unknowns that change which epics\n57\texist.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n60\t\n61\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (summary) | Epic(s) |\n62\t|-----|----------|----------------------|---------|\n63\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Tutorial gallery in the Dashboard with one-click launch into the user's project | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 |\n64\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated, tested tutorials covering the core journeys | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app), RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 (first pipeline) |\n65\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 |\n66\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation for gallery usage and tutorial contribution | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 |\n67\t\n68\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-2 is split across two\n69\tepics by component/team boundary (notebook tutorials vs. pipeline tutorial),\n70\tnot by priority.\n71\t\n72\t## Component and Team Mapping Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Owner teams are taken from `.context/architecture-context/` (Dashboard →\n75\t  RHOAI Dashboard; Notebooks → Workbenches; Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI\n76\t  Pipelines). The strategy has no Impacted Teams table.\n77\t- **E001 component mapping (non-obvious):** the packaging format spans both\n78\t  Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines tutorials and is consumed by the\n79\t  Dashboard. Assigned the single most-relevant canonical component `Notebooks`\n80\t  (five of the six tutorials are notebooks; the format's pinned-image concern\n81\t  is the workbench images maintained by the same team). The span is noted here\n82\t  per the component-name constraint.\n83\t- The \"first deployment\" and \"first RAG app\" tutorials are placed in the\n84\t  notebook tutorials epic (E003): the journeys are notebook-driven and the\n85\t  strategy's affected components include no model-serving component.\n86\t- E005 uses canonical component `Documentation` with a docs team; the\n87\t  Documentation component has no architecture-context file (it is a content\n88\t  process, not a code component), so no onboarding chain applies.\n89\t\n90\t## Health Warnings\n91\t\n92\t- **Missing strategy sections:** the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n93\t  Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n94\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Decomposition proceeded from the HLRs and\n95\t  problem statement; epic acceptance criteria were derived accordingly.\n96\t- **Priority inheritance on E001:** HLR-3 is P1, but the packaging format epic\n97\t  is P0 by inheritance — it transitively enables both P0 HLRs (HLR-1 and\n98\t  HLR-2). If the team intends the format to land after an initial un-packaged\n99\t  release, the tutorials and gallery would need rework to retrofit packaging;\n100\t  this decomposition assumes format-first to avoid that duplication.\n101\t- **Scope trap risk (recurring validation):** HLR-2 requires each tutorial to\n102\t  be \"tested against the current release\" and HLR-3 makes tutorials \"testable\n103\t  independently of Dashboard releases\", which implies re-validation on future\n104\t  releases. The strategy does not state where recurring validation executes\n105\t  (CI wiring, schedules). Scope is captured as the validation manifest within\n106\t  the packaging format plus per-release testing as an acceptance criterion;\n107\t  standing automation infrastructure is not scoped to any epic.\n108\t- **Out-of-scope boundary respected:** partner/community tutorial intake\n109\t  tooling and localization are excluded per the strategy; the contribution\n110\t  process is documented only (E005 scope).\n111\t\n112\t## Tiered Delivery\n113\t\n114\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing. All work is\n115\tintra-platform across existing, GA components (Dashboard, Notebooks, Data\n116\tScience Pipelines are all present in architecture context and Konflux\n117\tonboarded; no repo/konflux onboarding chains are needed).\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a24ffe3bc7ddb63f","agent_id":"af103264e5f155e9c","session_id":"93b0d1e1-8c2e-4425-b7ff-b40e259bbfcd","uuid":"cc6b3da8-44b3-4a2d-a304-ffb8bd7d0c74","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:43:36.649Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2fea8f0b61c6980","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
